orresponding to $T.$\n\nNote that the change of variables\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}},\\,v=xy\n$$\n\n \ngives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}u(x,y) \\\\ v(x,y)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo compute the required integral, we proceed as follows:\n\n**Step 1**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $D$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$ \n\nOur domain in the $uv$-plane is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,1\\le u\\le 16,\\,2\\le v\\le 5\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & \\frac{∂u}{∂y} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & \\frac{∂v}{∂y}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}-\\frac{2y}{{x}^{3}} & \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ y & \\text{ }\\text{ }x\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3y}{{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}={\\left(\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)}\\right)}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{\\left(-\\frac{3y}{{x}^{2}}\\right)}=-\\frac{1}{3u}.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 4**: Perform the change of variables:\n\nPerforming the change of variables, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}(xy)^{2}\\,dx\\,dy & ={∬}_{Δ}{v}^{2}|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={∬}_{Δ}{v}^{2}\\cdot |\\frac{1}{3u}|\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{2}^{5}{\\int }_{1}^{16}\\frac{{v}^{2}}{u}\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{2}^{5}{v}^{2}[{\\int }_{1}^{16}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u]\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{2}^{5}{v}^{2}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|\\,{|}_{1}^{16}]dv \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{2}^{5}{v}^{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡16-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1)\\,dv \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}{3}{\\int }_{2}^{5}{v}^{2}\\,dv \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}{v}^{3}\\,{|}_{2}^{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}{9}\\cdot (125-8) \\\\  & =26\\operatorname{ln}⁡4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186539379 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "088d3881-6f26-5c1e-8b70-605ffcbe6a13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4 \\ln{\\left(3 \\right)}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539357} {:answer/id #uuid "13d60485-67ff-563a-a2f9-a27075387c5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{112 \\ln{\\left(3 \\right)}}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539358} {:answer/id #uuid "4e49411c-8515-54df-bf3e-1b739c795ae9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{112 \\ln{\\left(3 \\right)}}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539367} {:answer/id #uuid "719b5cba-94f5-5e18-8818-62c388bfb5f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{112 \\ln{\\left(3 \\right)}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539375} {:answer/id #uuid "cef2c8c7-9728-5e8f-b345-f1a76f0182b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40 \\ln{\\left(3 \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539384}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4e49411c-8515-54df-bf3e-1b739c795ae9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{112 \\ln{\\left(3 \\right)}}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539367} :answer-field/id #uuid "58854fce-abbe-50be-9446-ce124d3d6e2f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539369}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a9bf5a72-2afe-55a9-8288-03e8e500cac8" :question/problem "Using the change of variables $u=\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}$ and $v=xy,$ evaluate the double integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}(xy)^{2}\\,dx\\,dy,\n$$\n\nwhere $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}\\le y\\le 9{x}^{2},\\,2\\le xy\\le 4\\}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's define a transformation $T$ as follows:\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane to our region $D$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\nTo compute the required integral, we can use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dx\\,dy={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(x(u,v),y(u,v))|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|du\\,dv\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$\n\nNote that the change of variables\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}},\\,v=xy\n$$\n\n \ngives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}u(x,y) \\\\ v(x,y)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo compute the required integral, we proceed as follows:\n\n**Step 1**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $D$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$ \n\nOur domain in the $uv$-plane is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,1\\le u\\le 9,\\,2\\le v\\le 4\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & \\frac{∂u}{∂y} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & \\frac{∂v}{∂y}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}-\\frac{2y}{{x}^{3}} & \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ y & \\text{ }\\text{ }x\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3y}{{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}={\\left(\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)}\\right)}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{\\left(-\\frac{3y}{{x}^{2}}\\right)}=-\\frac{1}{3u}.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 4**: Perform the change of variables:\n\nPerforming the change of variables, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}(xy)^{2}\\,dx\\,dy & ={∬}_{Δ}{v}^{2}|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={∬}_{Δ}{v}^{2}\\cdot |\\frac{1}{3u}|\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{2}^{4}{\\int }_{1}^{9}\\frac{{v}^{2}}{u}\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{2}^{4}{v}^{2}[{\\int }_{1}^{9}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u]\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{2}^{4}{v}^{2}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|\\,{|}_{1}^{9}]dv \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{2}^{4}{v}^{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡9-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1)\\,dv \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{3}{\\int }_{2}^{4}{v}^{2}\\,dv \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}{v}^{3}\\,{|}_{2}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{9}\\cdot (64-8) \\\\  & =\\frac{112\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186539380 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1760086a-7c09-5e8c-b8a1-c75d9fe9a51b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\ln(4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539359} {:answer/id #uuid "6a996faf-b917-5a49-b738-11415367209b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 14 \\ln(4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539373} {:answer/id #uuid "7ea0e4fa-607a-52bf-a6d1-09e1f76b57f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14\\operatorname{ln}⁡4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539377} {:answer/id #uuid "cf2b0b28-1110-5655-97fd-3599b3b30adf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "42 \\ln(4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539385} {:answer/id #uuid "d44bf487-a72f-5688-b79f-679c5c9843de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{85 \\ln(4)}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539386}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7ea0e4fa-607a-52bf-a6d1-09e1f76b57f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14\\operatorname{ln}⁡4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539377} :answer-field/id #uuid "e0c9be7b-466c-5bfe-beef-e661